## PgBouncer userlist.txt example
## Copy to /etc/pgbouncer/userlist.txt
## Each line: "<username>" "<password_or_md5_hash>"
##
## Plain text passwords are acceptable on secured servers.
## MD5 format: "md5" + md5(password + username) — no spaces
##
## To generate an md5 hash:
##   echo -n "md5$(echo -n 'PASSWORDUSERNAME' | md5sum | awk '{print $1}')"
##
## Example for user "appuser" with password "secret":
##   echo -n "md5$(echo -n 'secretappuser' | md5sum | awk '{print $1}')"

"appuser" "CHANGE_ME_OR_USE_MD5_HASH"
"pgb_exporter" "CHANGE_ME_OR_USE_MD5_HASH"
